From 134b6eaac2324ba83fe4d18a6c75913d557338ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:11:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] Bugfix: fix out-of-memory handling of `dgraphBand()`
 and `SCOTCH_dgraphBand()` [report R. Perry]

When the private data of the band graph could not be allocated, both
routines wrote their error flag into the NULL private array. The array
that collects the error flags of all processes was sized in `int`s and
overflowed when `Gnum`s are wider than `int`s. In `dgraphBand()`, the
frontier array was freed without having been allocated when a later
allocation failed, and the index array was freed with the base value
of the band graph after `dgraphFree()` had reset it, hence from a
wrong address when the base value is not zero. Errors in the halo
exchange, in the final build of the band graph and in the debug checks
returned without freeing anything.

Send the error flag from a local variable, size the error flag array
in `Gnum`s, attach the edge arrays to the band graph as soon as they
are allocated, and route all errors through cleanup labels, as in
`dgraphInduce2()`. Also fix the indentation of two lines.

Refs: DGR-09, API-17
